  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_efc3568c4299475f91d5adb3a813e16f",
      "statement": "celld makes two promises: exactly one node serves a cell at a time so two machines never write the same database, and celld does not answer a write until that write survives a failure so nothing acknowledged is lost.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/guarantees.md#L3-L7",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ed3f81b9871a035a35fd07d3e1bdd4890debea95468eaa07ae85f3df417c4aa8:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_30b604c3cf2b4c97a15241399d3981c2",
      "statement": "Each cell has one ownership record at cells/<cell>/own.json carrying the owner node and the epoch.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/ownership_store.rs#L288-L299",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e1b5873e52f78b5e353888f2973ab447e8bc1c705b27bc06a3cfd04498ccf900:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_cb9eb305c8364460a27b8d1a82c9d46d",
      "statement": "A node acquires a cell with a conditional write: a create when no record exists or a compare-and-swap on the previous etag, and the bucket accepts one such write so two nodes cannot acquire the same cell.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/ownership_store.rs#L401-L420",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9bdbbe13a62b4c9797188e72905829c2c4f920543857c2bcf62561f8a693a580:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_e598ef6d2fc242fbbbdf23351a6723ae",
      "statement": "An ambiguous acquire is re-read rather than retried blindly because it may have applied, but the number of reconciles per claim is bounded by MAX_ACQUIRE_RECONCILES (3) so a persistently unanswered store fails the request instead of spinning.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/lib.rs#L81-L96",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:96d3615d71fe7cf2fbef40007870eac2c093f53295570682460ce52120ec1efa:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_3bb337d6ccc948d7a55e4d47ce452e9f",
      "statement": "Every activation advances the epoch, so each owner replicates under a fresh epoch and an epoch never has two writers; the epoch in the object key under cells/<cell>/ltx/e<epoch>/ is the fence that keeps a stale owner's later writes in a superseded prefix.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/guarantees.md#L114-L128",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4266403b34060864e7dce422b45ba3bc833b3bbf5aa09321b0af00e113fbdb82:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_4afb0d82befd44b5a827d0f9212ba853",
      "statement": "A RestoreSpec carries the facts ownership resolution already decided: the epoch, whether the activation created epoch one, whether ownership was taken over, whether the local epoch remains authoritative, and the prior owner displaced.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/types.rs#L49-L70",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e96887004505982a8a1cb61a4d5d513ef2cc5b667fe97165a3f4643264ac8f5a:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_7c719275448a42658f8c2c61bbfa98b4",
      "statement": "The output gate is one choke point: nothing that reveals a cell's state may leave while the cell has a write it cannot prove durable, and the core stores the Channel route without branching on it so all channels use one rule.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/output_gate.rs#L3-L40",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:53f4d903ee08d3c69ca81eff4abdcfbb00a425217083f1ad035ac4be0187e95b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_963e9f38545847baa789430b5a68ffa8",
      "statement": "A write opens its own barrier and waits for a proof covering its position, while a read-only output joins the newest open barrier on its cell and a cell with nothing outstanding releases at once.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/output_gate.rs#L67-L95",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c922c5b92035a2b5c70fb428859b5e893c13875e6c019d4fda739eb7fbdf79ce:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d8a2454d4c3b4f36871ec5b84ab70755",
      "statement": "A write is acknowledged only when the replica proved a position covering the gated write; a shorter proof fails the write, and a bucket proof additionally requires an ownership read before anything is revealed.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/output_gate.rs#L167-L196",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:42681acc77860cbbc5e6e7d9efecfcdf36e532d4a04c98b0733e28f11be98e09:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_202d44ed4ad04e3b8164c204d285a0b7",
      "statement": "On a failed durability proof the cell resets: it stops serving writes the bucket may not hold and keeps no local snapshot, so the next activation restores from the bucket.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/output_gate.rs#L281-L284",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e17e35bf6b0f295f6c65a35bb6610a4eb696d5a72e9305b04b50d279802f84ff:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_88d4d5d04a76499c93c8c298fc8891ce",
      "statement": "In fleet mode the owner sends each write to one or two followers that must fsync it, and a takeover seals the prior node-log session before restoring so the stale owner cannot complete another fleet proof.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/guarantees.md#L144-L149",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:839841cce01f69a99e195c9304391596a5d8ae8fd968f7a5fd7ab4c49939ff89:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d28ad1146948496c90d46df0e112305b",
      "statement": "A node picks followers from other nodes and never counts itself, so a fleet needs two running nodes for a fleet proof; up to two followers give three copies in a fleet of three or more, the ensemble keeps acknowledging while one follower remains, and a node without an ensemble falls back to a bucket proof.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/guarantees.md#L151-L167",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:eb245ff4ad1ea390df353aa38d2ebb6a52afc2733b5578dff742499c2e66d139:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_5cd64f615e7b4bed99d9297a4090c749",
      "statement": "Each process session creates a conditional node-log record before its first fleet-durable acknowledgement, and a cold activation runs recovery when the prior owner's record is open or recovering, fencing it and uploading the followers' retained segments before it may restore.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/guarantees.md#L171-L183",
