      "id": "claim_830e0fb644de45daac414583efc0ba9f",
      "statement": "Acquiring the input gate happens during an event and is synchronous with the JS call that asks for it, nested blocks are counted rather than refused, and a holder that dies is abandoned so a cancelled request cannot shut the gate forever.",
